\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{A reflection of a calculus}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{Let #{L} be the weighted Laplacian of \ref{fdip-00PA}, with
derived form #{q_x} and bilinear form #{B_x} as in
\ref{fdip-00PB}. A \newvocab{reflection} of this calculus is an
involution #{\theta} of the vertices such that whenever
#{x\to y} is an edge, so is #{\theta x\to\theta y}, and
##{L(f\circ\theta)=(Lf)\circ\theta,\qquad
  \covwedge(f\circ\theta)=(\covwedge f)\circ\theta}
for every function #{f}. Thus #{\theta} commutes with #{L} and
with the exterior derivative.}
